.TH XQUEST 6 "2026-09-20" "1.1.1" "Games"
.SH NAME
xquest \- top-down arcade shooter (XQuest v1.3 SDL2 port)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B xquest
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xquest
is a faithful SDL2 port of XQuest v1.3, a fast-paced top-down arcade
shooter originally written for DOS by Mark Mackey in 1994.
.PP
Pilot a spaceship through 50 levels.
Collect all crystals on each level to open the exit gate, then fly
through it to advance.
Meanwhile, avoid or destroy up to 18 distinct enemy types and their
missiles, collect powerups, and use smart bombs strategically.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-scale " N"
Set the window to
.I N
times the game's 320x240 resolution (1 to 16), or
.B auto
to fit the display, which is the default. A requested scale is capped
at what fits on screen.
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Start fullscreen (borderless desktop fullscreen, no video mode switch).
.TP
.B \-\-windowed
Start windowed, whatever was saved from the last run.
.TP
.BI \-\-play " [FILE]"
Play back a demo, then return to the menu. Defaults to
.I xquest.dmo
in the config directory.
.TP
.BI \-\-record " [FILE]"
Record the next game to
.IR FILE .
.TP
.BI \-\-dump\-frames " FILE"
With
.BR \-\-play ,
write the raw 320x240 BGRA frames to
.I FILE
(or
.B \-
for standard output) as fast as possible, for encoding to video.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XQUEST_SCALE
A number or
.BR auto ,
same as
.BR \-\-scale .
.TP
.B XQUEST_FULLSCREEN
Any value but
.B 0
starts fullscreen.
.TP
.B XQUEST_DATA_DIR
Where to read the game data from, for a portable or relocated install.
.TP
.B XQUEST_CONFIG_DIR
Where to keep the per-user files listed below.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.B Arrow keys / WASD
Move the ship.
.TP
.B Left Shift / Right Shift / Numpad\~5
Brake (reduce velocity).
.TP
.B Space / Left mouse button
Fire.
.TP
.B Escape
Return to the main menu.
.TP
.B F11 / Alt+Enter
Toggle fullscreen.
.TP
.B Ctrl+plus / Ctrl+minus
Resize the window one step at a time.
.SH DIFFICULTY LEVELS
.TP
.B Wimp
Enemies are slower; ship bounces off walls.
.TP
.B Timid / Average / Tricky / Inhuman
Progressively faster enemies; contact with walls destroys the ship
(unless the Shield powerup is active).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/games/xquest/
Read-only game data (sprites, sounds, enemy definitions).
.TP
.I ~/.config/xquest/xquest.scr
Per-user high-score table (created automatically).
.TP
.I ~/.config/xquest/xquest.cfg
Per-user settings, in the 1994 original's exact text format.
.TP
.I ~/.config/xquest/xquest.win
Window size and fullscreen state, remembered between runs. Kept apart
from
.I xquest.cfg
so that file stays byte-compatible with the original.
.TP
.I ~/.config/xquest/xquest.dmo
Recorded demo, also used for attract mode.
.SH SEE ALSO
The original XQuest documentation is available in the original DOS
distribution (XQUEST.DOC).
.SH AUTHOR
